DESCRIPTION >
    Analytics: raw pageview rows over a date range with optional drill-down
    filters, feeding the /analytics/summary route's JS-side aggregation
    (unique visitors, top pages, top sources, AI sources, device/country
    breakdowns). Faithful 1:1 port of api/lib/posthog.js:129-146
    (`fetchPageviews`, shared by 5 call sites) as called from
    api/routes/analytics.js:187 (queryName 'summary', limit 10000).
    Tenant-scoped; prunes via (site_id, timestamp).

    IDENTITY CORRECTION (read carefully — the dispatch's assumption for this
    row was WRONG, verified against the actual source): the dispatch's rule
    #19b said these 5 fetchPageviews-based reads "dedup on BAG
    properties.anonymous_id (NOT distinct_id)". That is true for live.js:22
    (a genuinely different query) but NOT for this one. fetchPageviews'
    PAGEVIEW_FIELDS table (posthog.js:75-88) maps its OUTPUT column
    `anonymous_id` to the RAW `distinct_id` COLUMN, not to
    properties.anonymous_id — confirmed verbatim: `['anonymous_id',
    'distinct_id']`, with the file's own comment: "NOTE: server-routed
    events carry no session_id; visitor-dedup uses anonymous_id
    (distinct_id)." Porting this with JSONExtractString(properties,
    'anonymous_id') would have been WRONG and would have broken parity —
    the live query's "anonymous_id" IS distinct_id here. Ported as the typed
    distinct_id column (no JSONExtract, no cost concern — this is the
    canonical stitching key, already the sorting-key prefix).

    Typed-column translation (SCOPE_v3.md §2.6): properties.site_id ->
    site_id, event -> event_type, properties.page_url -> page_url,
    properties.referrer -> referrer, properties.utm_source -> utm_source,
    properties.utm_medium -> utm_medium, properties.utm_campaign ->
    utm_campaign, properties.country -> country, properties.device_type ->
    device_type, properties.browser_name -> browser_name, properties.
    ai_source -> ai_source (all Nullable per §2.6).
    JSON-BAG FIELD HIT (flagged): properties.os_name -> os_name is in §2.6's
    bag list (alongside browser_version/os_version), NOT a typed column —
    read via JSONExtractString(properties, 'os_name').

    OPTIONAL DRILL-DOWN FILTERS: the live route builds an arbitrary-length
    filter list from query params (parseFilters/buildPageviewFilterSql,
    analytics.js:29-48), ANDing together zero or more {type, value} pairs
    across 9 possible types (Page/Entry/Exit -> page_url ILIKE;
    Source -> referrer =; Country -> country =; Device -> device_type =;
    Browser -> browser_name =; OS -> os_name (bag) =; 'AI Source' ->
    ai_source =). Ported as 9 independent optional template params
    (filter_page/filter_entry/filter_exit/filter_source/filter_country/
    filter_device/filter_browser/filter_os/filter_ai_source), each ANDed in
    via `{% if defined(...) %}` when the caller supplies it. SIMPLIFICATION
    (flagged, not hidden): this supports one filter per type simultaneously,
    matching how every real caller in this codebase invokes it; it does NOT
    support the live code's theoretical (never-exercised in this app's UI)
    ability to pass TWO filters of the SAME type in one request.

    SHARED TEMPLATE — this pipe is structurally IDENTICAL to sources_ai.pipe,
    sources_ref.pipe, browsers.pipe, and os.pipe (all 5 are the same
    fetchPageviews call, differing only in the caller's default LIMIT and
    the runtime filter values) — same relationship as the alert_*/integ_*
    cross-file duplicates from earlier batches: authored separately per the
    dispatch ("one .pipe each"), not deduped, flagged here as a Phase-6
    consolidation candidate (a single parameterized pipe could serve all 5
    call sites).
    NOT YET PUSHED — validated read-only via `tb --cloud sql` only.

TOKEN "st_endpoint_read" READ

NODE summary_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        page_url AS url,
        referrer,
        utm_source,
        utm_medium,
        utm_campaign,
        country,
        device_type AS device,
        browser_name AS browser,
        JSONExtractString(properties, 'os_name') AS os,
        ai_source,
        distinct_id AS anonymous_id,
        timestamp
    FROM events
    WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
      AND event_type = '$pageview'
      AND timestamp >= toDateTime({{ String(date_from_ts, required=True) }})
      AND timestamp < toDateTime({{ String(date_to_ts, required=True) }})
      {% if defined(filter_page) %}
      AND page_url ILIKE concat('%', {{ String(filter_page, required=True) }}, '%')
      {% end %}
      {% if defined(filter_entry) %}
      AND page_url ILIKE concat('%', {{ String(filter_entry, required=True) }}, '%')
      {% end %}
      {% if defined(filter_exit) %}
      AND page_url ILIKE concat('%', {{ String(filter_exit, required=True) }}, '%')
      {% end %}
      {% if defined(filter_source) %}
      AND referrer = {{ String(filter_source, required=True) }}
      {% end %}
      {% if defined(filter_country) %}
      AND country = {{ String(filter_country, required=True) }}
      {% end %}
      {% if defined(filter_device) %}
      AND device_type = {{ String(filter_device, required=True) }}
      {% end %}
      {% if defined(filter_browser) %}
      AND browser_name = {{ String(filter_browser, required=True) }}
      {% end %}
      {% if defined(filter_os) %}
      AND JSONExtractString(properties, 'os_name') = {{ String(filter_os, required=True) }}
      {% end %}
      {% if defined(filter_ai_source) %}
      AND ai_source = {{ String(filter_ai_source, required=True) }}
      {% end %}
    ORDER BY timestamp DESC
    LIMIT {{ Int32(limit_val, 10000) }}

TYPE endpoint
